    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_ear.fix": "Set the MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY and SESSION_SECRET environment variables on your server, then restart.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eit.title": "Encryption in transit (TLS)",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eit.desc": "All data between users and Bee-Flow must travel over TLS (HTTPS).",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eit.fix": "Place Bee-Flow behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy and set TRUST_PROXY=1 so auditors can confirm TLS.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_dlp.title": "Data Loss Prevention active",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_dlp.desc": "PII detection, regex guardrails and content moderation reduce the risk that sensitive data leaks to external models.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_dlp.fix": "Open Security → Guardrails and turn on regex collections, PII detection and moderation.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_log.title": "Access / guardrail logging",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_log.desc": "GDPR Art. 32 expects ongoing monitoring. The guardrail_events log shows what was blocked, redacted or allowed.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_log.fix": "Ensure guardrails are enabled so events are produced. If logging is silent, DLP may be disabled.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art33.title": "Breach notification readiness",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art33.desc": "Art. 33 requires notifying the supervisory authority within 72 hours of a personal-data breach. We detect bulk decrypts as an early signal.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art33.fix": "Add at least one email under \"Breach notification recipients\" in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art37.title": "DPO appointed",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art37.desc": "A Data Protection Officer is mandatory when you process personal data at scale (Art. 37).",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art37.fix": "Fill in DPO name and email in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art12.title": "Privacy notice published",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art12.desc": "Data subjects must find, in plain language, how their data is processed (Art. 12-14).",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art12.fix": "Publish your privacy notice and paste its URL in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art44.title": "International transfers controlled",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art44.desc": "Using an external LLM exports personal data outside the EU. Art. 44-46 requires SCCs/DPA or equivalent safeguards.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art44.fix": "Either switch the agent(s) to self-hosted models, or register each external provider with a signed DPA/SCC in your records.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art50.title": "AI disclosure to users",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art50.desc": "The EU AI Act Art. 50 requires that end users are informed that they are interacting with an AI system.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art50.fix": "Add a line like \"You are chatting with an AI assistant\" to the system prompt or welcome banner of each published agent.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art13.title": "Transparency: agent described",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art13.desc": "Art. 13 expects users to understand the purpose, limitations and provider of the AI system.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art13.fix": "Fill in a meaningful description (30+ characters) for each agent in Admin → Agents.",

